1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,283
A little party for our team.

2
00:00:03,533 --> 00:00:08,008
Decorations, cake, six happy people. I have a
perfect plan.

3
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:10,195
Leave room for surprises.

4
00:00:10,445 --> 00:00:14,497
Could the surprises come after dessert this
time, please?

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,343
Six plates. One for each of us.

6
00:00:18,593 --> 00:00:22,186
Aunt Rose is stopping by, but she cannot stay.

7
00:00:22,436 --> 00:00:24,529
Her chair gets a vacation.

8
00:00:24,779 --> 00:00:29,498
Then the six places are for us. We can still
say hello.

9
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,706
We have one strawberry. Just in case.

10
00:00:33,956 --> 00:00:36,316
A very small emergency cake.

11
00:00:36,566 --> 00:00:39,772
Let us wait for the real one.

12
00:00:40,022 --> 00:00:44,497
Couldn't hurt to keep the little one on
standby, though.

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,607
A little ribbon for your family party.

14
00:00:48,857 --> 00:00:52,374
Thank you, Rose. Can you stay a moment?

15
00:00:52,624 --> 00:00:54,501
Just a moment, sister.

16
00:00:54,751 --> 00:00:59,498
Good. You can see what the ribbon's for before
you go.

17
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,900
Mine keeps becoming a knot.

18
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:05,980
Give the loops a little room.

19
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:08,200
People need that too.

20
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:13,430
There. It looks more like a bow when I loosen
it.

21
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,968
Today I have checked absolutely everything.

22
00:01:18,218 --> 00:01:22,186
Then you will know where to start if something
changes.

23
00:01:22,436 --> 00:01:24,904
That sounds like a useful plan.

24
00:01:25,154 --> 00:01:29,497
I think I'll keep the checklist where I can
find it.

25
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,620
We will save you a story about the party.

26
00:01:34,870 --> 00:01:37,700
That travels better than cake. Goodbye!

27
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:39,920
See you soon, Rose.

28
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:44,290
I'll remember the funny parts to tell you
later.

29
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,116
A bow at the right address.

30
00:01:48,366 --> 00:01:51,380
That is an excellent place for it.

31
00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:55,041
And the bell can still do its job.

32
00:01:55,291 --> 00:01:59,498
Good. We want to hear it when the cake comes.

33
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,900
The entrance is still clear.

34
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:05,550
The party can get in.

35
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,770
So can the people.

36
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:12,140
Good. No one has to step over our decorations.

37
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,900
No ribbon under anyone’s feet.

38
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:20,980
No mystery leftovers on the counter.

39
00:02:21,230 --> 00:02:24,060
Now we can enjoy the room.

40
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:28,430
I can still see the bow from the doorway.

41
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,283
Our address is fourteen Maple Lane.

42
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:35,470
Blue door, number fourteen.

43
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:39,772
Even I cannot confuse the door with the cake.

44
00:02:40,022 --> 00:02:44,497
I'd like to see the cake try wearing our bow.

45
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,197
Fourteen Maple Lane. Delivery around two.

46
00:02:48,447 --> 00:02:50,324
Correct address, correct cake.

47
00:02:50,574 --> 00:02:54,911
The confirmation is correct. We will check the
delivery too.

48
00:02:55,161 --> 00:02:59,498
Fair. An order number can't ring our bell by
itself.

49
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:02,900
A space for the box.

50
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:06,840
The strawberry has a very large neighbor
coming.

51
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:09,490
They will both stay cool.

52
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:14,290
Good. Let's keep that space open till the
doorbell rings.

53
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:19,468
I will not check the cake until I see it.

54
00:03:19,718 --> 00:03:22,936
There is room for that on the list.

55
00:03:23,186 --> 00:03:25,279
And room in the fridge.

56
00:03:25,529 --> 00:03:29,497
Then the checkmark waits until the box is
actually here.

57
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:33,283
Dear cake, welcome to our table.

58
00:03:33,533 --> 00:03:35,893
It may need directions first.

59
00:03:36,143 --> 00:03:39,349
We will welcome it when it arrives.

60
00:03:39,599 --> 00:03:44,497
Okay. I'll save my welcome speech until it can
hear me.

61
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,470
A very punctual napkin.

62
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,120
There is a delivery message.

63
00:03:50,370 --> 00:03:53,200
Let us see what it says.

64
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:57,570
A message before a doorbell? That's worth a
look.

65
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,860
It says delivered at two-oh-six.

66
00:04:03,110 --> 00:04:06,316
Then why is the cake not here?

67
00:04:06,566 --> 00:04:09,349
Let us check before we guess.

68
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:14,497
The time tells us when. We still need to know
where.

69
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,900
No box on the step.

70
00:04:18,150 --> 00:04:20,980
Not even a very small one.

71
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:24,060
Good. That is one place checked.

72
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:29,290
Well, at least we're sure it isn't behind our
own door.

73
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,654
No cake in the fridge.

74
00:04:32,904 --> 00:04:35,058
No cake beside the board.

75
00:04:35,308 --> 00:04:39,778
Then we are looking for a delivery, not a
hidden dessert.

76
00:04:40,028 --> 00:04:44,498
Good. The whole box wouldn't fit inside that
little dish anyway.

77
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:48,514
I wanted one afternoon without a mix-up.

78
00:04:48,764 --> 00:04:51,778
We can still have a good afternoon.

79
00:04:52,028 --> 00:04:55,042
First, let us find out what happened.

80
00:04:55,292 --> 00:04:59,499
All right. I'll start by listening to what we
know.

81
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,470
The order numbers match.

82
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,980
So the message is about our cake.

83
00:05:06,230 --> 00:05:09,490
A clue. Much better than a complaint.

84
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:14,290
Good. We know which order to ask the bakery
about.

85
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,654
Did somebody steal our party?

86
00:05:17,904 --> 00:05:22,760
We do not know that. A delivery could go to
another door.

87
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:24,778
There is a photo.

88
00:05:25,028 --> 00:05:29,498
Let's look. Maybe the step will tell us where
it went.

89
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,470
That door is green.

90
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,520
Ours is blue.

91
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:38,030
Then the box was photographed somewhere else.

92
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:43,260
That's the first clue we can see without
reading any numbers.

93
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:48,283
No bow in the photo either.

94
00:05:48,533 --> 00:05:50,893
Our cake missed the decorations.

95
00:05:51,143 --> 00:05:55,195
The picture can help us ask a clear question.

96
00:05:55,445 --> 00:05:59,497
Good. We can describe what's actually in the
picture.

97
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,470
Should I order another?

98
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,550
First check where this one went.

99
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:09,060
One missing cake is enough to investigate.

100
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:14,290
Fair. Six people don't need two cakes turning
up at once.

101
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:20,022
Our order is marked delivered, but the photo
shows another door.

102
00:06:20,272 --> 00:06:21,906
Clear and polite.

103
00:06:22,156 --> 00:06:25,116
With actual facts. I like this version.

104
00:06:25,366 --> 00:06:29,498
Good. That gives support something they can
check for us.

105
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,654
The emergency strawberry is ready.

106
00:06:32,904 --> 00:06:35,830
It is one strawberry for six people.

107
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:39,392
Let us give the cake a chance first.

108
00:06:39,642 --> 00:06:44,498
Good. Cutting one berry six ways sounds like a
very small party.

109
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:48,197
There must be several green doors.

110
00:06:48,447 --> 00:06:51,144
We need the right green door.

111
00:06:51,394 --> 00:06:54,911
And we can ask before entering anyone’s space.

112
00:06:55,161 --> 00:06:59,498
Right. A green door is a clue, not an
invitation.

113
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,300
A leaf-shaped knocker.

114
00:07:02,550 --> 00:07:06,240
And that little hedge. I know that hedge.

115
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:09,320
Let us check the number too.

116
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:13,690
Good. Lots of leaves look alike from this
distance.

117
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:18,116
I cannot read that last digit.

118
00:07:18,366 --> 00:07:20,585
Then do not guess it.

119
00:07:20,835 --> 00:07:24,644
We can compare the actual number at the door.

120
00:07:24,894 --> 00:07:29,498
Fair. One blurry digit isn't enough to knock
on someone's door.

121
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,900
The driver recorded number eighteen.

122
00:07:33,150 --> 00:07:35,120
Our confirmation says fourteen.

123
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:38,630
Now we have two numbers to compare.

124
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:43,430
Good. Eighteen is something we can actually go
and check.

125
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:50,022
We can ask, did a cake for number fourteen
arrive here?

126
00:07:50,272 --> 00:07:53,232
Better than, where is our entire party?

127
00:07:53,482 --> 00:07:55,116
Much better.

128
00:07:55,366 --> 00:07:59,498
And it sounds friendlier if you're on the
other side.

129
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,900
We will all go together.

130
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:06,410
Just along this sidewalk. No road crossing.

131
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,490
And straight back if nobody answers.

132
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:13,860
Good. I'll keep my eyes on the house numbers.

133
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:18,760
Blue door behind us, green door ahead.

134
00:08:19,010 --> 00:08:21,840
We are checking the actual signs.

135
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:24,920
The sidewalk is doing excellent work.

136
00:08:25,170 --> 00:08:29,290
It can't read the numbers for us, though, Dad.

137
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,470
The same low hedge.

138
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:35,980
I recognized it without asking a statue.

139
00:08:36,230 --> 00:08:39,060
A useful improvement over the park.

140
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:43,860
I much prefer hedges. They don't pretend to
know directions.

141
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,300
Number eighteen.

142
00:08:47,550 --> 00:08:49,520
Different number, different door.

143
00:08:49,770 --> 00:08:52,600
The delivery photo matches this place.

144
00:08:52,850 --> 00:08:56,970
We should still ask whose box it really is.

145
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:03,330
Can we peek through the hedge?

146
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:06,410
We can ring the bell instead.

147
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:08,460
Much less scratchy.

148
00:09:08,710 --> 00:09:12,830
Good. I'll keep my nose out of that hedge.

149
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,760
This is the door in the photograph.

150
00:09:19,010 --> 00:09:20,980
One question, calmly asked.

151
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:23,200
We are all here.

152
00:09:23,450 --> 00:09:28,860
And the box in that photo hasn't told us whose
it is.

153
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:32,300
Now we wait.

154
00:09:32,550 --> 00:09:34,520
I can do that.

155
00:09:34,770 --> 00:09:37,170
You have had pancake practice.

156
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:41,540
Good. Apparently that pan was preparing me for
doorbells.

157
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:48,197
Maybe the cake answered the door.

158
00:09:48,447 --> 00:09:51,144
Cakes are very poor at doorbells.

159
00:09:51,394 --> 00:09:54,501
Let us give our neighbor a moment.

160
00:09:54,751 --> 00:09:59,498
Fine. I'll keep the welcome speech till we
have an answer.

161
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:04,256
If nobody is home, we will ask the bakery
again.

162
00:10:04,506 --> 00:10:07,552
Yes. We do not need to look around.

163
00:10:07,802 --> 00:10:10,138
We have already found useful clues.

164
00:10:10,388 --> 00:10:14,499
Yes. Knowing where the photo was taken gives
us a start.

165
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:17,300
Someone is coming.

166
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:19,350
Good afternoon.

167
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,570
Thank you for answering.

168
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:26,370
We only need a moment to ask about the
delivery.

169
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,148
Hello. We are from number fourteen.

170
00:10:33,398 --> 00:10:38,460
We are checking a delivery that may have
reached the wrong door.

171
00:10:38,710 --> 00:10:40,394
A cake delivery.

172
00:10:40,644 --> 00:10:44,499
The photo looks like the step outside your
door.

173
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:49,129
A white bakery box with a red seal.

174
00:10:49,379 --> 00:10:52,585
The photo shows it beside this door.

175
00:10:52,835 --> 00:10:55,195
We have the order confirmation.

176
00:10:55,445 --> 00:10:59,497
We can show the matching number if that helps.

177
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:03,952
Did a cake for number fourteen arrive here?

178
00:11:04,202 --> 00:11:08,057
We think there may have been a number mix-up.

179
00:11:08,307 --> 00:11:09,991
No hurry.

180
00:11:10,241 --> 00:11:14,498
We brought our confirmation if you'd like to
compare it.

181
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,900
That sounds like a fridge.

182
00:11:18,150 --> 00:11:21,410
Let us hear what our neighbor says.

183
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:24,490
Yes. We still need to check.

184
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:28,860
Good. A fridge sound can't tell us what's
inside.

185
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:33,330
Same order number, same white box.

186
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:35,980
That will help identify it.

187
00:11:36,230 --> 00:11:38,630
And explain the mistake clearly.

188
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:43,860
That'll tell us more than just the color of
the door.

189
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:49,190
Thank you for helping us sort this out.

190
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:52,270
Our plates are waiting very patiently.

191
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:54,320
So are we.

192
00:11:54,570 --> 00:11:59,120
My plate's got a bit more patience than my
stomach.

193
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:03,994
My perfect plan did not include asking for
help.

194
00:12:04,244 --> 00:12:07,009
There is still time to add that.

195
00:12:07,259 --> 00:12:10,389
It is a useful line on any list.

196
00:12:10,639 --> 00:12:14,498
I'm adding that one to the plan in my head.

197
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,300
A white box.

198
00:12:17,550 --> 00:12:19,520
With a red seal.

199
00:12:19,770 --> 00:12:23,890
Let us check it before we carry it home.

200
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:28,690
Good. A white box alone could hold somebody
else's dessert.

201
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,900
That is our order number.

202
00:12:33,150 --> 00:12:35,120
And our cake description.

203
00:12:35,370 --> 00:12:38,630
Now we can ask about the label.

204
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:43,000
Good. The handwriting and our address still
need comparing.

205
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,787
The order ends in ten-C.

206
00:12:48,037 --> 00:12:49,914
So does the sticker.

207
00:12:50,164 --> 00:12:55,321
The plain round cake. We have checked more
than the box color.

208
00:12:55,571 --> 00:12:59,498
Good. Now let's hear what happened when it
arrived.

209
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:04,893
This came to eighteen. I put it straight in
the fridge.

210
00:13:05,143 --> 00:13:07,639
Thank you for keeping it cool.

211
00:13:07,889 --> 00:13:09,476
We appreciate that.

212
00:13:09,726 --> 00:13:14,498
Dinner's a lot easier to sort out when
somebody remembers the delivery.

213
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:18,630
The label looked like eighteen to the driver.

214
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,551
Our confirmation says fourteen.

215
00:13:20,801 --> 00:13:24,660
A small mark sent a large cake on a visit.

216
00:13:24,910 --> 00:13:29,499
Good. We can give the bakery the number that
caused the mix-up.

217
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:32,860
I have not opened it.

218
00:13:33,110 --> 00:13:35,047
The seal is intact.

219
00:13:35,297 --> 00:13:38,926
Thank you. We will take it straight home.

220
00:13:39,176 --> 00:13:44,497
Good. That red seal looks just like the one in
the photo.

221
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:48,116
Here you are. Enjoy your party.

222
00:13:48,366 --> 00:13:51,777
Thank you for being a very good neighbor.

223
00:13:52,027 --> 00:13:55,041
Our cake has had quite a trip.

224
00:13:55,291 --> 00:13:59,498
And a very kind person looked after it. Thank
you.

225
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,134
Thank you again.

226
00:14:02,384 --> 00:14:06,125
We will tell the bakery it is safely
recovered.

227
00:14:06,375 --> 00:14:09,726
And we will check every digit next time.

228
00:14:09,976 --> 00:14:14,498
Good. I want the bakery to know which address
caused it.

229
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:18,330
Does it need a ticket home?

230
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:21,410
Just a steady pair of hands.

231
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:24,490
I have checked both of mine.

232
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:28,860
Good. My job can be keeping the sidewalk
clear.

233
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,470
Blue door, number fourteen.

234
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:35,120
At last, the correct entrance.

235
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:37,770
Straight to the fridge first.

236
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:43,000
Understood. This stop is only for dropping off
our cold passenger.

237
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:48,607
A safe place while we get ready.

238
00:14:48,857 --> 00:14:51,964
The party can wait two more minutes.

239
00:14:52,214 --> 00:14:54,911
We have found something worth celebrating.

240
00:14:55,161 --> 00:14:59,498
And the little strawberry's got its neighbor
back at last.

241
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:04,309
Recovered safely from number eighteen. Please
check the label.

242
00:15:04,559 --> 00:15:06,778
Fourteen is still our address.

243
00:15:07,028 --> 00:15:09,644
And thank you for the help.

244
00:15:09,894 --> 00:15:14,498
Good. They'll know they can close the search
for our cake.

245
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,900
Clean hands before we serve.

246
00:15:18,150 --> 00:15:21,410
The cake traveled farther than we did.

247
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:24,060
Its box did the traveling.

248
00:15:24,310 --> 00:15:29,290
And everybody who handled that box can wash up
for dessert.

249
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:34,093
May I have the emergency strawberry with my
slice?

250
00:15:34,343 --> 00:15:37,186
Yes. It can retire from emergency duty.

251
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:39,904
One berry, one very important job.

252
00:15:40,154 --> 00:15:44,497
I think it deserves a very good seat on my
plate.

253
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,330
Here is our guest of honor.

254
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:50,550
Same order, right house.

255
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:54,490
And still cool. We can serve it now.

256
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:59,290
I'll save my welcome till we actually have our
slices.

257
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,900
The box is finally empty.

258
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:06,840
The cake has a much better view now.

259
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:09,490
And space for six servings.

260
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:13,860
Good. Every plate has a person waiting for it.

261
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,300
Six equal slices.

262
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:19,520
No four-or-forty problem today.

263
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,600
Just six people sharing one cake.

264
00:16:22,850 --> 00:16:27,400
I like this math. Everybody gets the very same
share.

265
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:33,330
One for Dan, one for Leo.

266
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,550
A very successful delivery.

267
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:38,630
This time we saw it arrive.

268
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:43,860
Good. I can confirm this slice is at the right
address.

269
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,900
Two left on the board.

270
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:50,980
One for Nina, one for Max.

271
00:16:51,230 --> 00:16:54,060
Exactly. No one has to guess.

272
00:16:54,310 --> 00:16:58,430
Good. I can count them from my own place.

273
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,900
My slice has an assistant.

274
00:17:03,150 --> 00:17:04,950
The emergency strawberry.

275
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:07,600
Six slices. Everyone has one.

276
00:17:07,850 --> 00:17:13,260
Good. It was a long trip for this little bit
of cake.

277
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:19,970
The cake is with the family. The sharp tools
stay here.

278
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:22,760
That is a good final check.

279
00:17:23,010 --> 00:17:25,936
Can I call the job done now?

280
00:17:26,186 --> 00:17:29,498
Yes. Come sit down and enjoy your slice.

281
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:32,900
I wanted a perfect party.

282
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:36,410
You made room for a real one.

283
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:39,060
We found the cake together.

284
00:17:39,310 --> 00:17:44,290
That's the part I want to remember when we
tell it.

285
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,900
To this very helpful team.

286
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,120
And our kind neighbor.

287
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:52,770
And checking the whole address.

288
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:58,000
And the person who noticed the green door in
the picture.

289
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,116
Did the family party start yet?

290
00:18:03,366 --> 00:18:06,777
Almost, Dad. Our cake visited the neighbor
first.

291
00:18:07,027 --> 00:18:09,643
It came back with a story.

292
00:18:09,893 --> 00:18:14,497
We'll tell you the whole thing once we taste
it, Ed.

293
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:19,427
A clear address is better than a lucky guess.

294
00:18:19,677 --> 00:18:22,784
We have been collecting evidence for that.

295
00:18:23,034 --> 00:18:24,911
Thanks, Dad. Talk soon.

296
00:18:25,161 --> 00:18:29,498
Bye, Grandpa. We even read the little print
this time.

297
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,300
Sweet. Not sour.

298
00:18:32,550 --> 00:18:34,950
And no flowers in it.

299
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,600
Just a very welcome cake.

300
00:18:37,850 --> 00:18:41,970
This one definitely got the right kind of
flour.

301
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:48,550
The ribbons were not the best part.

302
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:50,484
What was?

303
00:18:50,734 --> 00:18:54,186
Everyone staying with the problem. And with
me.

304
00:18:54,436 --> 00:18:59,498
I'd stay with you even if the strawberry were
all we had.

305
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:03,760
You do not have to guess alone.

306
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:06,840
Even when your checklist looks impressive.

307
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:08,890
Especially then.

308
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:13,690
A second pair of eyes doesn't take up much
room.

309
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:18,760
Emergency strawberry, thank you for your
service.

310
00:19:19,010 --> 00:19:20,980
A very small hero.

311
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:23,030
With excellent timing.

312
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:28,260
Good. Nobody else had to share one tiny berry
six ways.

313
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:35,050
Would anyone like to stay right here for a
while?

314
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,100
Yes.

315
00:19:37,350 --> 00:19:39,150
No directions required.

316
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:43,950
Fine by me. I know exactly where my plate is.

317
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,283
The party found the right house.

318
00:19:48,533 --> 00:19:51,739
It had the right people all along.

319
00:19:51,989 --> 00:19:56,041
Everybody has a slice. Who's going to tell
Rose?

320
00:19:56,291 --> 00:19:59,497
Me. I'll start with the little strawberry.
